 <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:49:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/34] Metal: -mgpu wiring and a refusing 2-D gate

Adds metal/metalinversion.{h,mm}: the 2-D inversion (GPU gridding + ducc0's own
forward chain) as a library usable by the gridder, plus a -mgpu setting that
routes WGridder::AddInversionMsImplementation through it.

The backend refuses unless it does exactly the same maths as the ducc0 call it
replaces: Metal present, no image shift, and the Fresnel criterion
pi*|w|*lambda*(l^2+m^2) <= 0.1 rad at the image corners. Every refusal reports
why. Multi-channel data is handled like ducc0's 2-D path: one grid, chain and
correction per channel, accumulated into the image.

Measured on the real sets it refuses everywhere - LOFAR 3C196 has w_max = 495 km
(6.8 rad of w-error even at a 4 arcmin field); the MWA snapshot gives 0.70 rad.
A 2-D backend cannot serve a real wide-field image, so the next milestone is
w-layers.

